      "message": "Haha, I was looking at this, too. I think that technically, the correct fix is to make index be unsigned right away (declared as uint32_t, and call readUInt instead of read32). That would make the subtraction safe, and keep the existing behavior that negative values (ie, very large unsigned values) would actually fail the read - by calling validate(false).\n\nThe version you wrote means that having a negative (very large) index behaves the same as 0, which means \"we serialized a null object, so return that\". Ultimately, it\u0027s going to work just as well, though - the corrupted buffer is probably going to fail validation shortly after this...",
